 "notes": "Continuation of Table XV Part II(B) Tri and poly-lingualism. Subsidiary column headers on header pages of this part print 'Dogri.', 'Panjabi.', 'Kashmiri.' (leaf 266 adds letters (B),(C),(D)); recorded as Dogri/Panjabi/Kashmiri. Rows printed nil ('....') in every column are omitted; subsidiary triples all-nil are omitted. Remarks: wrapped lines joined; a word broken across lines ('langu-'/'ages.' or 'langu'/'ages.') is rejoined as 'languages.'. Page 264 (header page, same column heads as leaf 272). Ladakh District: Ladakh Tehsil and Skardu Tehsil (both tehsil labels faintly printed, read 'Lada[k]h Tehsil' and 'Skar[d]u Tehsil'; the bracketed letters are faint but the names are unambiguous). Frontier Ilaqas (printed 'Frontier Ilaqas', no tehsil level) begins at the foot of the page and continues on leaf 275. No subsidiary-language figures and no remarks on this page. Faint/broken type read with tight zoom: Ladakh Tehsil Ladakhi Females 16,686 (16667+16686=33353); Skardu Balti Males 51,159; Frontier Ilaqas Kashmiri Persons 54 (broken 4; 46+8=54). Rows all-nil omitted: Ladakh Gojari, Western Pahari, Chabhali, Shina; Skardu Gojari, Western Pahari, Chabhali, Pothwari."
